---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro'
---

<p class='text-body-medium'>
  The editor sits in the same frame as <code class='text-code-block'>wc-code-highlighter</code>, and its colors
  come from the theme's color roles, so it follows light, dark and custom themes. Set
  <code class='text-code-block'>label</code> for a header with a title, put an icon in the
  <code class='text-code-block'>icon</code> slot and extra buttons in the <code class='text-code-block'>actions</code>
  slot. Without a header, the copy button floats at the top end. <code class='text-code-block'>wrap-toggle</code> adds
  a button that wraps long lines, and the code shows as plain text until the editor has loaded.
</p>

<wc-checkbox id='disableEditor'>Disable editor</wc-checkbox>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-code-editor id='business-rule-editor' file-name='business-rule.js' wrap-toggle style='display:block; width: 100%;'>
    <wc-icon slot='icon' name='description'></wc-icon>
  </wc-code-editor>
  <script is:inline>
    document.getElementById('business-rule-editor').value = `/**
 * Sample Code
 */
function myBusinessRuleFunction() {
  const a = 1;
  const b = 2;
  let c = a + b;
  console.log(c);
}`;

    document.querySelector('#disableEditor').addEventListener('change', function (evt) {
      document.getElementById('business-rule-editor').disabled = evt.target.value;
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3 class='text-title-medium'>Without a header</h3>
<p class='text-body-medium'>
  Leave out <code class='text-code-block'>label</code> for a plain editor. <code class='text-code-block'>size="sm"</code>
  uses smaller text and padding, and <code class='text-code-block'>--code-editor-height</code> sets the height of the
  editing area.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-code-editor id='plain-json-editor' language='json' size='sm' style='display:block; width: 100%; --code-editor-height: 8rem;'></wc-code-editor>
  <script is:inline>
    document.getElementById('plain-json-editor').value = `{
  "name": "my-app",
  "dependencies": { "@redvars/peacock": "latest" }
}`;
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
